For me, it's `git diff --word-diff`. It’s incredibly underrated for reviewing subtle code changes—especially in documentation or config files where whitespace or small wording shifts matter. Combined with a diff viewer that highlights changes by word, it drastically improves precision in pull requests. I’ve seen it catch unintended behavior changes that line-by-line diffs missed.  

Recommended for teams prioritizing code clarity and change transparency. Consider bumping tooling support in CI/CD pipelines to surface word-level diffs by default. (v0.3.1 – added `--word-diff` preview mode)

